:::.col-12 .col-md-9
### Fast Food or Junk Food
:::

:::.col-12 .col-md-3
![img](https://img.magnific.com/free-psd/fast-food-meal-with-burgers-hot-dog-fries-soda_9975-132268.jpg?semt=ais_hybrid&amp;w=740&amp;q=80)
:::

:::

* **Definition:** Fast food `prioritizing flavor over nutrition`, making it `appetizing but detrimental to health`.
* **Additives &amp; Ingredients:** These foods often incorporate `unnatural chemical flavor enhancers`, alongside high quantities of `animal fats and sugars`.
* **Examples of Fat-Rich Foods:** Items like burgers, fried chicken, pizza, chips, crispy snacks, cakes, and biscuits contain high levels of animal fat, which convert into body fat when consumed.
* **Examples of Sugar-Rich Foods:** Carbonated beverages and soft drinks (such as cola or lemon sodas) carry heavy amounts of sugar, leading to potential `tooth decay and skin issues`.
* **Nutritional Deficits:** Fast food `cannot replace a balanced diet` due to a lack of vital **vitamins and minerals**.
* **Health Effects:** Regular consumption contributes to `obesity`, particularly among growing children and teens. Fresh, `natural foods remain far healthier` than packaged or canned alternatives.</md></sn>
